{"availability":"available","full":"sktime/tserve","name":"tserve","description":"Time Series serving (TServe): local inference server for foundation models","category":"Education","language":"Python","stars":10,"forks":1,"created":"2026-07-27T12:29:13Z","updated":"2026-09-28T14:50:21Z","license":"BSD-3-Clause","branch":"main","homepage":"https://tserve.readthedocs.io/","topics":["deep-learning","docker","forecasting","foundation-models","gpu","huggingface","inference","machine-learning","model-serving","pretrained-models","python","pytorch","serving","sktime","time-series","time-series-forecasting","timeseries","transformers"],"demo":null,"color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T10:45:07.783Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-03T10:45:07.783Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-03T10:45:07.783Z","lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T10:45:07.783Z","discoveredVia":[],"metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T10:45:07.783Z","stars":10,"forks":1}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Time series serving for foundation models. TServe loads models such as Chronos, TimesFM, Moirai, TTM, and TiRex once, keeps them in memory, and answers forecast requests over HTTP.","Each model family ships its own package, input format, and loading code. sktime wraps them as forecasters with one common interface, and TServe runs those forecasters as a server behind a single request: a table of past values and a horizon. Trying another model means changing one field, not rewriting your pipeline.","TServe is a server you run on your own hardware, not a hosted API. How it works · Docker Hub"],"features":["Over 100 checkpoints. Each family has its own Docker tag or pip extra, for CPU or GPU. Catalog · Capabilities","Loaded once, kept warm. Weights download and load at startup, so each request pays only for inference.","Native tables in Python. The Client takes a dict, pandas, polars, or pyarrow table and returns predictions in the same type.","A dashboard in the browser. GET / plots a forecast from a sample series or your own CSV. What you can do","Your own sktime models. Serve a configured forecaster, a saved .zip, or a craft spec next to the catalog models."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/sktime/tserve/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"64cc6794e58c2b3aeb04d02d115cbd5f34f62ed28cf58c34f63439e8e2726e11","extractedAt":"2026-10-03T10:45:07.783Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T10:45:07.783Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Time series serving for foundation models. TServe loads models such as Chronos, TimesFM, Moirai, TTM, and TiRex once, keeps them in memory, and answers forecast requests over HTTP.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/sktime/tserve/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"64cc6794e58c2b3aeb04d02d115cbd5f34f62ed28cf58c34f63439e8e2726e11","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/sktime/tserve/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-03T10:45:07.783Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-09-28T14:50:21Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/sktime/tserve/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-03T10:45:07.783Z","hash":"64cc6794e58c2b3aeb04d02d115cbd5f34f62ed28cf58c34f63439e8e2726e11","originalBytes":16273,"storedBytes":16273,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["chronos","model","models","tserve","server","docker","bolt","timesfm","client","moirai","own","predict","python","gpu","json","load","past","same","sktime","start","family","forecast","mantis","prediction","tirex","what","any","dashboard","each","extra","hub","install","naive","post","request","sales","series","table","tafsut","tag","ttm","arrow","bash","column","full","get","image","images","kronos","license","loaded","loads","one","pandas","pip","python.","quantiles","run","send","startup","them","timestamp","weights","api","base","capabilities","catalog","command","covariates","development","first","how","models.","name","page","posts","predictions","process","requests","row",